Description: store_scalar: bind value_w only for writable attributes
 HdbPPMySQL::store_scalar() puts the value_w column into the INSERT, and counts
 a parameter for it, only when the attribute is writable (write_type !=
 Tango::READ). The bind loop nevertheless bound value_w for every row, so for
 a read-only scalar each row bound one MYSQL_BIND beyond its slot, and the
 last row one beyond the end of the variable-length MYSQL_BIND array on the
 stack. AddressSanitizer reports it as a dynamic-stack-buffer-overflow (WRITE
 of size 8 in bind_value<Tango::DevState>, from store_scalar<Tango::DevState>);
 without it the EventSubscriber dies with SIGSEGV on the first archive event of
 a read-only DevState attribute. store_array() already guards the same bind
 this way.
Author: Falak Sher <45312905+falaksherpk@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-10-24
---
--- a/src/LibHdb++MySQL.cpp
+++ b/src/LibHdb++MySQL.cpp
@@ -1895,8 +1895,11 @@
 				bind_value(plog_bind[plog_bind_ind],mysql_value_type,value_data[2*chunk_idx+0],value_data_len[2*chunk_idx+0],is_null[3*chunk_idx+0],is_unsigned);
 				plog_bind_ind++;
 
-				bind_value(plog_bind[plog_bind_ind],mysql_value_type,value_data[2*chunk_idx+1],value_data_len[2*chunk_idx+1],is_null[3*chunk_idx+1],is_unsigned);
-				plog_bind_ind++;
+				if(!(write_type == Tango::READ))	//RW: value_w is in the query only then
+				{
+					bind_value(plog_bind[plog_bind_ind],mysql_value_type,value_data[2*chunk_idx+1],value_data_len[2*chunk_idx+1],is_null[3*chunk_idx+1],is_unsigned);
+					plog_bind_ind++;
+				}
 			}
 
 			if (mysql_stmt_bind_param(pstmt, plog_bind))
